         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 3 polynomial needs the values through order 3: \\( f(-1) = -3 \\), \\( f'(-1) = 5 \\), \\( f''(-1) = 2 \\), \\( f'''(-1) = 0 \\). The value of order 4 is not used.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{-3}{0!} = -3 \\), \\( \\frac{5}{1!} = 5 \\), \\( \\frac{2}{2!} = 1 \\), \\( \\frac{0}{3!} = 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
